WEBVTT

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.360
Mokoyama, returning as a panda man,

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:08.580
brought along with him the ultimate weapon,
Super Baking Powder, and challenged Azuma.

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:12.960
Faced with the difficulty of making
bread steamed with hot spring water,

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.790
the Pantasia team had a hard fight ahead of them, but...

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.920
The water is filled with bamboo leaves!

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.840
Oh, this smells good.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.340
That’s it! This smell!

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:25.840
This is it!

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.350
We did it, Kawachi, Kanmuri!

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:31.770
I-It’s true!

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.350
There were three explosions!

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:35.640
It’s done.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:37.730
Well, then.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:41.190
Oh no!

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.530
Everyone, down!

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:43.350
What?

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.900
The Panda’s bread is an awesome bread!

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:49.610
It’s just explosive!

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:51.450
It’s a good bread...

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:58.200
Kuro-yan exploded three times, and
has been blown into a million tiny pieces!

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.380
I was pretending to show a reaction.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:02.960
During that time, I secretly swapped my body on stage.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:04.260
Let’s go.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:07.930
Th-That’s...

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:09.510
Roumen...

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.010
No, it’s a Noh mask!

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:13.680
Kuro-yan’s face has become a Roumen...

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.930
I mean a Noh mask!

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:18.310
Th-That’s really creepy!

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:29.160
A truly deeply mellow fragrance and faint sweetness.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.330
I, Kuroyanagi, stand in awe.

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:35.030
Victor: Pantasia!

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:36.240
All right!

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:37.990
We did it!

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:38.990
Yeah, we did!

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:41.340
Using bamboo along with his Roumen technique,

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.300
Kazuma’s secret plan was truly explosive.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:46.720
And it won against the Panda’s Triple Alps Steamed Bread.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.300
Well then, we will now begin the eighth match.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:55.060
Participants from Pantasia, step forward!

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:01.560
There are only two matches left in Yakitate!! 9.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:05.820
I’m sure that St. Pierre will do their best
to send forth a fearsome opponent.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.820
But, no matter who our opponent is, we won’t lose!

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.320
We will win and get back Pantasia!

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:14.570
Next, would the participant
from St. Pierre step forward!

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.080
Th-That’s Yukino!

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:21.950
Isn’t it Azusagawa Yukino?!

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.340
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.170
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.470
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:33.970
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:39.060
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:42.810
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:53.570
I want this voice to reach you, even though it’s still a tiny song.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:59.740
That’s because I have the feeling that something’s gonna start.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:14.840
As I was cowering, muffling my voice, the tears that I shed

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:23.430
probably helped me notice that

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:29.310
I’ve almost forgotten how to believe.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:38.200
The future that I painted (I will fulfill it)

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:43.570
Looking up to the clear skies,

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:50.710
I begin to run once again. Someday, I want to dye

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:56.500
that white sky with my colors.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:03.510
I’m going to fly as far as possible, shining like a marble,

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:07.890
unfolding these wings of mine.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:16.790
The sun vs. the blizzard!!

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:18.790
The ultimate tart showdown!

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:25.180
I-Isn’t that Yukino?

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:27.090
Why is she here?

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.570
Th-That’s...

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:31.450
You little...

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:35.810
How many times do I have to tell you
not to talk when I’m talking?!

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:39.190
If you do it again, I’ll shave off
every hair you have on your bodies!

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:41.690
E-Every hair on our bodies?!

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:44.900
We’re very sorry.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:46.280
We won’t do it again.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:47.950
We’re truly repentant!

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:49.910
Well, as long as you understand.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:54.040
Well then, let’s move on to
choosing the city for our topic.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:57.290
Would the participant from St. Pierre
step forward and choose a panel.

00:04:58.170 --> 00:04:59.040
Six.

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:01.030
Open panel #6.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:03.260
Looks like it is Tomiura.

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:07.430
But, this city’s name is colored red.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:10.000
The topic for this city has been decided in advance.

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:12.000
Now, let’s flip it once again.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:14.680
Tart?

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.750
And let’s zoom in.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.710
Tomiura is a city in the Awa district of Chiba prefecture.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:25.300
It is famous for producing
strawberries and Kenjou loquats,

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.470
which are loquats of high quality that even to
this day are presented to the Imperial household.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:34.970
You are to use these marvelous fruits to
create a tart that can be presented proudly.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:36.230
That is all.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.860
That really surprised me.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.700
To think that she’s our next opponent...

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:51.280
Yeah...

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:54.450
But then, that means we’ve just had
some unexpected luck come our way.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:56.120
She may be fearsome as a person,

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:59.370
but when it comes to baking bread,
we wouldn’t lose to such a woman.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:01.300
No, that’s not the case.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:07.380
However, yeast are ultimately germs, aren’t they?

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:12.680
It’s true that Azusagawa Yukino is the
kind of person who calls bread yeast a germ.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:15.350
We’d be safe in saying that she has
absolutely no talent in baking bread.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:17.420
But on the other hand,

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:22.860
she possesses the ultimate gift to make tarts, which is our topic this time.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.730
In contrast to the Solar Hands that we possess,

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.240
she possesses the ultimate gift
coveted by patisserie chefs.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.900
The Blizzard Hands!

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:37.790
The Blizzard Hands?!

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:41.000
But that was surprising.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:45.210
To think that Yukino had such a gift...

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:47.380
But, Kanmuri...

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:50.510
Why is it advantageous to have
cold hands when making tarts?

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:53.010
That’s because tart dough
is not fermented.

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:57.100
Among tart doughs,
there is a variety called futage.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:01.100
All you do is add butter into the
thin, non-fermented dough and fold it.

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:04.020
Since it’s non-fermented, your
hands don’t need to be warm.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:08.360
It is advantageous to have cold hands, as it will
keep the butter from melting for a longer time.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:12.070
Things like tarts, where you add fruit
to the dough, are all about crispiness.

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:15.530
So, the more skillfully you add in the butter,
the bigger the advantage you have.

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:16.700
I see...

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:18.160
B-But wait a moment.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:19.040
Still...

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:24.210
Even Azuma can make a
many-hundred-layer croissant, right?

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:28.800
The only differences between
croissant dough and tart dough

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:32.130
are the amount of butter you add in
and whether or not you ferment it, right?

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:36.220
If you make the croissant into the
dough for a tart, won’t it be crispy then?

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:38.470
That is certainly a possibility.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:42.140
But, while that may be pretty
rare for a fermented croissant dough,

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:44.340
it’s normal for tart dough,

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:47.820
which is folded without fermenting,
to have many hundred layers.

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:52.360
Unlike tart dough, which can be stretched infinitely thin since it’s not fermented,

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:55.610
croissant dough is made after the
dough has fermented and expanded.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.910
So there is a limit to how thin
you can make it by stretching.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:02.120
Only after going to great lengths can
you make that many layers in a croissant.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:03.500
And it absolutely can’t have more layers than a tart.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.000
I-I see.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.420
Also, even if you manage to
make a greater number of layers,

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:13.220
Yukino has yet another secret technique.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:16.970
A legendary technique that can be
performed only by people with cold hands.

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:18.010
The Reverse Folding Technique.

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:19.930
R-Reverse Folding?!

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:27.860
What is this?!

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:30.240
Isn’t this the match locale,
Tomiura of Chiba prefecture?!

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:34.240
City of Tomiura, Awa District, Chiba Prefecture

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:41.620
Wh-Why are we suddenly in the match locale?

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:45.660
Weren’t we just in front of the
Great Tokyo Television station?

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:47.710
Looks like we got here
before we knew it.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:50.290
Chiba is right next to Tokyo, after all.

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:51.170
It’s close by.

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:55.090
Are you making fun of me
because I’m from Kansai and not Tokyo?!

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:57.720
Nope, we’re just shortening things.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:00.220
Nobody wants to see the travel scenes, after all...

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:03.220
W-Well, that might be true.

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:06.230
So, what kind of super technique is it?

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:08.230
That Reverse Folding thing...

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:10.020
Putting it simply,

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:13.730
it is a technique where the dough is enveloped
in butter, even at its outermost ends.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:18.490
Normally, tarts and croissants are
made by wrapping butter inside the dough,

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:20.740
but in the case of Reverse Folding you do the opposite.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.950
You wrap the dough in butter.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:27.960
By doing this, you can wrap the outermost ends of the dough with butter as well.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:31.960
So, it’s possible to increase the
crispiness of the dough even further.

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:35.380
It goes without saying that
this is impossible

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:37.680
for anyone whose hands aren’t cold enough
to fold the butter so that it doesn’t melt.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:38.970
It is a high-level technique.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:41.180
H-How can this be...

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:44.560
To think that woman had
such a technique...

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:48.480
Where are we this time?!

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:51.190
Where have we been brought to?!

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:53.900
Geez, what the hell are you
talking about?!

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:55.360
We’re at the loquat market.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:56.740
The loquat market.

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:58.990
M-Market?

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:00.910
We’re just shortening the time.

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:02.320
Shortening it.

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:06.160
There’s no point in worrying
about our opponent after all.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:09.000
First, we have to think about
obtaining the specialty products

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:12.500
and deciding how to use them to make a delicious tart.

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:13.920
N-No...

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:17.210
That’s not what I’m worrying about.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:25.310
Damn geezer.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:27.270
You only have loquats preserved in brown sugar?!

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:28.600
What the hell do you mean?!

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.440
I have a match in three days.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:32.520
It’s useless telling me that.

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.900
You can’t get fresh loquats in this season.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:36.440
I can’t give you something I don’t have.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:40.700
All we have are loquats that have been preserved
in brown sugar syrup for long-term preservation.

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:43.200
Like I care about that!

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:46.700
Then why don’t you just plant
some and raise them right away?!

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:48.540
You’re asking for the impossible!

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:49.830
Stop that, Yukino!

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:51.540
What are you doing to
an elderly person?!

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:56.760
Well, look who we have here.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:59.720
It’s the cockroaches from Pantasia!

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:01.760
You’ve come to buy loquats too, right?

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:04.970
But it’s too bad...

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:09.270
It looks like it’s the wrong season
for the famous Kenjou loquats.

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:13.770
All they have here are these filthy
loquats, preserved in brown sugar

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:16.780
and put in these ridiculous
octopus pots for preservation.

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:20.280
My loquats are <i>not</i> filthy.

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:21.450
Yeah, that’s right!

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:23.410
Then, why don’t <i>you</i> use them?

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:26.910
I’ll use the other specialty product, strawberries.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:29.080
Bye bye then, Mr. Cockroach.

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.010
Are you hurt, Mister?

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.970
My body is all right.

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:51.430
But, I’m mortified.

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:54.690
While they may be preserved,

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:59.940
the loquats that I prepared so diligently
don’t deserve to be spoken of in that manner.

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:01.320
Mister...

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.030
Please, young man.

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:06.990
From what I hear, you’re going to have
a match with her on a TV program, right?

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:11.200
Is it not possible for you to
use my loquats and defeat her?

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:18.040
I know that fruit is more delicious when fresh.

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:20.680
I know that I’m asking for something unreasonable.

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:23.920
But my loquats are not filthy!

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:26.180
I want her to know that!

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:30.760
Please? It is the wish of a lifetime, young man.

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:37.350
All right, Mister.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:39.230
I’ll use these loquats.

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:40.650
I’ll defeat her with these!

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:42.650
Really?!

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:44.400
Yeah, of course!

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:46.570
A-Azuma-kun...

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:47.910
Azuma...

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:49.910
Please, young men!

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:51.290
Loquat Market
Please, young men!

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:54.750
Please take revenge for me!
Loquat Market

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:55.170
Loquat Market

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:58.000
Yep! Leave it to us!

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:03.130
But, is this really all right?

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:08.350
It’s not that I don’t understand your
sympathizing with him, Azuma-kun...

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:10.600
But, at the topic of making tarts,

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:13.310
Yukino is already at an
advantage due to her cold hands.

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:15.860
And that woman will be using fresh strawberries.

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:19.650
Of course, I don’t think that
they are filthy or anything...

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:23.110
But, preserved loquats have
absolutely no chance of winning.

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:24.610
That’s right, Azuma.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:29.240
It’s a given that using fresh fruit for a tart is best.

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:30.990
It’s not too late yet.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:34.380
Let’s apologize to the old man
and come up with another way.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:36.790
No, that won’t do.

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:39.420
I’m definitely going to use these loquats.

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:44.250
B-But being stubborn about this
won’t help much if we lose!

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:44.850
So...

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:46.220
I won’t lose.

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:48.100
Not if I take up the challenge
with croissants.

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:52.760
But, didn’t we just talk about this at
the Great Tokyo Television station?

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:57.730
Not even your many-hundred-layer
croissant can win against Yukino’s tart.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:00.480
I’m not fighting her with <i>that</i> croissant.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:03.400
I’ll be taking on the challenge with the Super Tart <i>Japan</i>.

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:06.240
With the Super Black Loquat Croissant!

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:08.740
B-Black Loquat Croissant?!

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:12.950
Hey, wh-where’s this now?!

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:15.620
The match location!

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:19.370
A-And why is it suddenly the day of the match now?

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:22.170
Isn’t the match usually three days
after the location is announced?

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:23.960
Looks like Azuma-kun did it.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.980
This time, we didn’t just fly to the
next place, we went ahead in time, too.

00:14:26.980 --> 00:14:30.220
W-Well, this isn’t quite the time to be impressed, is it...

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:33.470
It’s probably because Azuma-kun
is really serious this time.

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:35.680
Whether you’re a baker or not,

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:40.390
what’s most important is to care
about the people who eat your food.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:42.200
In other words,
your regard for other people.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:46.440
He holds more regard for others than most people.

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:52.570
I’m sure that his strong regard for the old man
will work in ways that we can’t even imagine.

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:54.660
That’s probably what made time fly ahead.

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:59.120
Well, I understand that it’s a
heartwarming story and all...

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:01.210
But as far as I’m concerned,
I’m just disturbed by the fact that

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:04.670
three days of my life just went by and
I have absolutely no memory of them.

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:07.420
Wh-What is it now?!

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:15.760
Hey, aren’t you the old man from the loquat market?!

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:19.640
It looks like Azuma-kun’s regard
transported the old man as well.

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:21.560
Wh-What was that?!

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:25.110
You must be surprised at the sudden turn of events.

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:27.320
This is the location of the match.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:31.070
The details will be explained
by this person here from Kansai.

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:32.610
So, please be at ease.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:35.700
Hey, wait a minute!

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:38.540
Well, I’m off to help Azuma-kun.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:42.670
Hurry up.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.420
5. 4. 3.

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:47.290
Well then,

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:51.130
we will now begin the eighth match
of Yakitate!! 9, here at Tomiura!

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:53.010
Begin!

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:02.730
That was quite a turn of events,

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:05.700
but now that we’re all here,
there’s nothing we can do about it.

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:07.820
I’ll leave all the rest to you.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:09.200
I believe in you, Azuma.

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:12.150
You’re a spectator again,
Kawachi-san?

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:15.860
Oh, Tsukino. And Manager!

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:19.710
Oh, you came too, Meister-han?

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:20.740
Yes.

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:25.670
I believe that as an official of
Pantasia, it is my responsibility

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:30.460
to watch over these last two matches of
Yakitate!! 9 that are to decide Pantasia’s fate.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:32.340
I guess that’s true.

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:34.510
Have a good time watching.

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:35.050
Okay.

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:38.930
Wh-What’s with that woman?!

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:43.980
She’s folding the butter with her
bare hands, but it’s not melting at all!

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:45.980
How in the world is she folding it?!

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:48.860
Th-That’s truly amazing.

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:52.110
I’ve seen many a baker, but...

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:55.990
It’s the first time I’ve seen someone
who can handle butter like that.

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:58.870
Far from melting,

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:01.870
it almost looks like the butter is hardening.

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:03.950
She truly has the Blizzard Hands.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:06.580
I-I wonder if Azuma-san
will be all right...?

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:10.880
At this rate,
she’ll make the ultimate tart!

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:13.260
I don’t know if he’ll be all right, but...

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:16.380
There’s no mistaking the fact that
he’s at a tremendous disadvantage.

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:17.970
N-No way...

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:20.930
Th-This is bad...

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:24.060
Even Manager just passed a pessimistic comment.

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:25.890
At this rate, we’ll...

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:29.190
Did you see that,
you little cockroaches?

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:30.690
This is my power.

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:32.780
You’re no match for me!

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:39.620
I’ll trample you to a pulp!

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:44.630
Wh-What?

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:46.870
Wh-What’s with that dough?!

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:50.170
I’ve never seen dough that can stretch so much!

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:53.000
Wh-What is that stretchy dough?!

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:54.670
Even I’ve never seen anything like that!

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:58.630
Way back when Azuma made
the double gluten dough, it...

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:04.180
But, this one stretches even more than that! It’s a dough with the ultimate extensibility!

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:09.310
Manager! How in the world did
Azuma make such an extensible dough?!

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:11.020
He’s using flour with high protein...

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:13.440
No, super-high protein content.

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:16.320
F... Flour with super-high protein content?

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:18.660
Wh-What the hell is that?

00:18:19.070 --> 00:18:23.660
Put simply, it is flour with even
more protein content than hard flour.

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:26.830
M-More protein content
than hard flour?

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:28.710
Does such a flour even exist?

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:29.670
Yep.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.710
Based on protein content,

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:37.170
flours are classified as soft, all-purpose, and hard.

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:42.850
But actually, flours with high protein content
and super-high protein content also exist.

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:47.730
But, if the protein content is too high,
it’s harder to get the dough to ferment.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:49.100
Also, it becomes hard to knead.

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:51.190
So, a regular person cannot use it.

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:56.730
It is something that only people who possess
the Solar Hands, like Azuma-kun, can use.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:18:58.490
I see...

00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:00.450
To think that something amazing like that existed...

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:03.870
But, the theme this time is tarts, right?

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:06.200
He needs to be making a crispy crust.

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:09.200
So, why is he making that kind of extensible dough?

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:12.040
Uh... Yeah, even I don’t know that.

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:13.830
Oh I see!

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:15.430
He’s doing something crazy!

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:20.130
Both of you,
look at his dough carefully!

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:21.880
That’s...

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:24.550
What does this mean?!

00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:26.890
Azuma’s dough
has suddenly disappeared!

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:28.640
Look a little more carefully.

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:30.860
It’s not like his dough has disappeared.

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:35.400
He’s stretched that sticky dough
to its absolute limit to make

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.900
a perfectly transparent dough!

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:39.110
I-I see!

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.150
If it’s just regular fermented dough,

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:43.160
then there’s a limit to how much you can stretch it.

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:44.910
But if it’s that extensible a dough,

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:47.620
then you can extend it as much as
you like, just like a sticky rice cake.

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:52.630
With this, it’s unmistakable that he’ll
be able to make a thin and crispy crust!

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:56.630
It’s for this reason that Azuma used the
super-high protein content flour, right?

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:57.540
Yep.

00:19:57.550 --> 00:20:02.340
With this, he might be able to
surpass the crispiness of Yukino’s crust!

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:05.140
So, it looks like the two crusts
are at about equal levels now.

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:07.390
All right!

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:08.850
You did it, Azuma!

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:12.180
Impressive, Azuma-kun.

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:13.850
And that is just how it should be.

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:19.860
Now you’ve gone and done it,
you little cockroach!

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:23.150
But... No matter how good your crust is,

00:20:23.150 --> 00:20:26.570
all you have are those filthy
loquats preserved in brown sugar.

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:27.870
You have no hope of winning.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:31.870
Looks like it’s finished baking.

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:40.380
Now that the baking is done,
all I have to do is add the strawberries.

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:45.930
If I make the judge eat it
before the crispiness disappears,

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:47.220
I’m sure to win.

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:48.050
All right!

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:51.360
I’m done!

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:52.680
Wh-What?!

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:55.520
O-Oh no!

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:57.360
What’s the matter, Manager?

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:59.690
Whether it’s a tart or a croissant,

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:02.440
the pie-type, crispy crust is
crispiest when it’s just baked,

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:04.870
and definitely more delicious if eaten immediately.

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:09.370
But... both have finished
making the tart at the same time!

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:14.120
It’s going to become a race to see
who can make Kuroyanagi eat it first!

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:15.000
What was that?!

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:24.010
In that case, eat both together!

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:52.950
C... Could it be that I asked for
something that I shouldn’t have?

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:55.160
Th-This is bad, guys!

00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:56.710
Wh-What is it this time?

00:21:56.710 --> 00:22:00.040
To make him eat two breads at the same time...

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:01.420
Something terrible is going to happen.

00:22:17.020 --> 00:22:20.150
We are all going to be pulled into this reaction.

00:22:20.150 --> 00:22:21.740
Wh-What was that?

00:22:25.320 --> 00:22:26.860
Wh-What’s...

00:22:27.240 --> 00:22:30.860
What’s going to happen to us?!

00:22:36.110 --> 00:22:44.000
Robbie, come on out to the sound of the voice calling you.

00:22:44.160 --> 00:22:51.920
Robbie, you were crying all by yourself.

00:22:52.140 --> 00:23:00.310
Robbie, the eyes in your heart...

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:03.780
what is it that they reflect?

00:23:03.980 --> 00:23:07.200
...Is it “Who am I?”...

00:23:07.560 --> 00:23:14.990
The other side of the mirage flickers faintly.

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:23.540
Anywhere is fine, as long as it’s not here.

00:23:24.540 --> 00:23:32.300
My dancing heart is reborn as a marble time and again.

00:23:32.550 --> 00:23:36.380
The colors I just filled in were yours.

00:23:36.380 --> 00:23:40.300
It’s not something that will finish with a turn. Be load.

00:23:40.470 --> 00:23:48.280
Just like your joy, try letting your tears flow.

00:23:48.530 --> 00:23:52.320
See? The world is filled in with your colors.

00:23:52.400 --> 00:23:58.990
Like a tumble, do the best of you.

00:24:05.950 --> 00:24:07.240
What is this?!

00:24:07.240 --> 00:24:09.200
Did a new program start suddenly?

00:24:09.200 --> 00:24:10.620
What are you talking about?

00:24:10.620 --> 00:24:12.200
Come, let’s move on quickly.

00:24:12.200 --> 00:24:14.310
It’s the start of a new adventure.

00:24:14.310 --> 00:24:15.560
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:15.560 --> 00:24:17.580
This is the path I must take!?

00:24:17.580 --> 00:24:18.750
The Road of the Loquat!

00:24:18.750 --> 00:24:19.890
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.340 --> 00:24:22.650
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.650 --> 00:24:25.090
The pastry that represents France, the tart.

00:24:25.090 --> 00:24:28.300
The origin of the name comes from “tourte,” a
disk-shaped, pie-type dessert from ancient Rome.

00:24:28.300 --> 00:24:31.670
Small versions of tarts are called tartlets.

00:24:32.100 --> 00:24:34.390
Oh?!
